The quantity the code means is "the lanes whose output rows are below group_heads", which is group_heads / ROWS_PER_LANE_4 lanes (ROWS_PER_LANE_4 is defined at line 167 for exactly this relation: "lane l of u holds tile columns 4*l..4*l+3, which become 4 consecutive output rows"). The code instead compares against one named value and lists the other three lanes by hand. The else-branch (lane 0 only) is right only because the only other accepted value is 4. Reading cost: the reader must check two facts the line does not state, that 16 heads means lanes 0..3 and that every non-16 value accepted by group_heads_ok means lane 0 alone, and must consult group_heads_ok to confirm the second. Proposed replacement, which keeps the 4-head instantiation's emitted code (lane 0 only) and the 16-head one (lanes 0..3):

