judged.body:
Rule 2 (a comment does not repeat a Note) and Rule 4 (line-to-code mapping). Classification: anchored fact. Lines 161-162 ("the kernel writes only the group_heads query rows, so `s` needs only group_heads rows") are amx_attn_iface.hpp:107-110 word for word. Mapping of the HEAD text: lines 158-159 -> the value -12345.f and the fill loop (175-179); line 160 -> the check loop (210-214); lines 160-162 -> the Note (restated). Proposed text (3 lines):

```
// A value no dot product of the fixture produces (|q.k| < 128). check_qk writes
// it into every score row and requires rows group_heads..15 to keep it, which
// pins the s[group_heads] contract of Note [Tile stores write 16 rows].
```
Mapping of the proposed text: line 1 -> the constant value and the fill loop; line 2 -> the check loop; line 3 -> the Note pointer that owns the contract.

Rule 2 (do not restate). The pack contract comment carries the padding fact in two places that the diff both rewrote. Lines 192-194 give it as the precondition: "with columns group_heads..15 of every panel already zero: this call writes columns 0..group_heads-1 only". Lines 198-199 give it again inside the layout description: "(columns 0..group_heads-1 = the heads, the rest zero padding)". The second parenthetical adds nothing the precondition and the index formula on 200-201 do not already say (q_head ranges over the heads). The existing finding at line 195 covers only the added sentence "For 16 heads every column is written, so that precondition is empty"; this second statement of the same fact was not flagged. Reading cost: a 15-line contract where the reader meets the padding rule twice and checks whether the two statements differ. Fix: shorten line 198-199 to
// `packed` layout: 4 panels, one per 32-dim step of the head; each panel is
// 16 dim-pair rows x 16 query columns x 2 paired values:
so that lines 192-194 are the single owner of the padding precondition.

Rule 2 (do not restate identifiers). The query-fill comment, new in this diff, says "The offset step is 1/16" on line 144 while line 145 declares `constexpr float HEAD_OFFSET_STEP_0_0625 = 0.0625f;` (1/16 = 0.0625, the value the name carries). Line 142 says "its own offset (i / head_size)" while line 146 computes `static_cast<float>(i / head_size) * HEAD_OFFSET_STEP_0_0625`. The confirmed finding at line 142 covers only the duplicated "exact in bf16"; these two identifier restatements are a separate cut in the same comment and were not named. What survives is the one fact the code does not say: why each head gets its own offset (a pack that permutes or drops heads cannot pass) and that the largest value, 2.6875 for head 15, is exact in bf16. Proposed replacement for lines 142-144 (absorbs the line-142 fix too):
    // A per-head offset makes a pack that permutes or drops heads fail. Every
    // value is exact in bf16 (head 15 peaks at 2.6875).
Verified: 1 + 15 * 0.0625 + 3 * 0.25 = 2.6875 = 1.01011b x 2^1, 5 fraction bits, inside bf16's 7.

corrections:
Replace "peaks at" with a literal verb in the proposed text:
    // A per-head offset makes a pack that permutes or drops heads fail. Every
    // value is exact in bf16 (head 15 reaches 2.6875).
Also note in the comment that this replacement absorbs the line-142 fix, so the author applies one edit, not two.

