comments.body:
tron-code-review: The gate test refuses shapes just outside the old limit but none just outside the new upper limit [nit].

Rule: boundary model shapes, check dimensions at the supported limits and just outside them. The rows at HEAD refuse kv_mul 2 and head 64 (both from BASE) and kv_mul 8 (new):

```
constexpr size_t KV_MUL_8 = 8;
STATIC_REQUIRE_FALSE(eligible<tron::bf16>(HEAD_SIZE_128, KV_MUL_8));
```

Nothing refuses a kv_mul (query heads per KV head) above 16. A future edit of `group_heads_ok` (amx_attn_iface.hpp:152-154) to `g == GROUP_HEADS_4 || g >= GROUP_HEADS_16` would keep every existing STATIC_REQUIRE green. It would admit kv_mul 32, for which no kernel is instantiated (templates declared in the header, instantiated only at amx_attn.cpp:333-350), so a model reaching the dispatch would fail at link time. No tron model has kv_mul 32 today, so this guards a future edit, not a current defect.

Proposed fix, after line 121, compile-time cost only:

```cpp
  constexpr size_t KV_MUL_32 = 32;
  STATIC_REQUIRE_FALSE(eligible<tron::bf16>(HEAD_SIZE_128, KV_MUL_32));
```

And extend the comment on lines 118-119 with "and nothing above 16".

tron-code-review: The "padding stays zero" comment states a precondition that the QK kernel does not need, so a reader may think the result depends on it [fwiw].

HEAD lines 1552-1554:

```
// resize() zero-fills new slots and the packer writes only the kv_mul
// live columns of each slot, so the padding it relies on stays zero
// (see the pack contract in amx_attn_iface.hpp).
```

The comment is true as written. One `self_attention<model>` instance has one geometry, so one kv_mul (query heads per KV head), and its `attn` scratchpad vector is not shared with an instance of another group size. Still, the result does not rely on the padding. Each column of the QK tile depends on its own packed-Q column only (`_tile_dpbf16ps` accumulates K[token].Q[column]), and the transposing store writes rows 0..group_heads-1 only [src/tron/kernels/amx_attn.cpp:255-260]. Stale padding columns would produce discarded values.

Reading cost: a maintainer may keep the zero-fill for correctness when it is only a conservative contract. Optional fix, comment only: say the kernel's result rows depend on columns 0..kv_mul-1 only, and keep the zero contract in amx_attn_iface.hpp:193-196 as the tested convention (t_amx_numerics.cpp:150 checks it).
